## 1. Plugin Manifest Schema

### Format: `plugin.yaml` (or `.json`)

Every plugin MUST include a manifest at its root declaring capabilities, dependencies, and metadata.

```yaml
# plugin.yaml - REQUIRED
apiVersion: "plugins.reporting.io/v1"
kind: "Plugin"

# Identity & Discovery
metadata:
  id: "com.company.datasource.salesforce"  # Reverse-domain notation, globally unique
  name: "Salesforce Data Source"
  description: "Fetch reports and data from Salesforce"
  version: "1.2.3"                          # SemVer required
  author: "sales-platform-team@company.com"
  homepage: "https://internal-wiki.company.com/plugins/salesforce"
  repository: "https://git.company.com/plugins/salesforce"
  license: "Apache-2.0"

# Framework Compatibility
requirements:
  minFrameworkVersion: "2.0.0"             # Earliest compatible framework version
  maxFrameworkVersion: "3.0.0"             # null = no upper bound (recommended)
  requiredAPIVersions: ["data.v2", "ui.v1"] # Must declare all versioned APIs used

# Plugin Capabilities: What this plugin provides
capabilities:
  - type: "datasource"
    id: "salesforce"
    exports: ["SalesforceConnector"]       # Main class/function names
    config:
      schema:
        properties:
          instanceUrl:
            type: "string"
            description: "Salesforce instance URL"
            required: true
          clientId:
            type: "string"
            description: "OAuth2 client ID"
            required: true
          clientSecret:
            type: "string"
            description: "OAuth2 client secret (stored securely)"
            required: true
            sensitive: true                # Framework won't log this

  - type: "visualization"
    id: "sankey-chart"
    exports: ["SankeyVisualization"]
    config:
      schema:
        properties:
          nodePadding:
            type: "number"
            default: 50
          colorScheme:
            type: "string"
            enum: ["viridis", "plasma", "cool"]
            default: "viridis"

  - type: "transformer"
    id: "currency-normalizer"
    exports: ["CurrencyNormalizer"]
    config: {}

# Dependencies on other plugins
dependencies:
  - id: "com.company.security.oauth2"
    versionRange: ">=1.0.0,<2.0.0"         # SemVer range
    required: true                          # false = optional, feature degrades gracefully

  - id: "com.company.shared.logging"
    versionRange: ">=1.0.0"
    required: false

# Permissions: What resources this plugin can access
permissions:
  - resource: "network"
    actions: ["http:GET", "http:POST"]     # Sandbox restricts unless granted
    scope: "https://salesforce.com/*"

  - resource: "filesystem"
    actions: ["read"]
    scope: "/tmp/plugin-cache"

  - resource: "memory"
    limit: "512MB"                          # Runtime enforcement

  - resource: "cpu"
    limit: "50%"                            # Runtime enforcement

  - resource: "api"
    actions: ["data.v2:query", "data.v2:aggregate", "ui.v1:notify"]

# Hooks this plugin subscribes to
hooks:
  load: "index.onLoad"                      # Called when plugin loads
  unload: "index.onUnload"                  # Called before unloading
  beforeQuery: "index.beforeQuery"          # Optional, data processing hook
  afterQuery: "index.afterQuery"

# Entry points
main: "dist/index.js"                       # Main bundle (transpiled to ES2020+)
types: "dist/index.d.ts"                   # TypeScript definitions for consumers

# Versioning & Stability
stability: "stable"                         # stable | beta | alpha
changelog:
  - version: "1.2.3"
    date: "2026-09-15"
    notes: "Fixed OAuth2 token refresh bug"
  - version: "1.2.2"
    date: "2026-09-01"
    notes: "Added batch query support"

# Security Baseline
security:
  auditedAt: "2026-08-01"
  auditedBy: "security-team@company.com"
  issues: []                                # Known CVEs or issues
  requiresReview: false
```

### Schema Validation Rules

- `metadata.id`: Must match regex `^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9\-]*\.[a-z0-9][a-z0-9\-]*\..*[a-z0-9]$`
- `version`: SemVer 2.0 format required
- `capabilities[].type`: Must be from registry of known types (datasource, visualization, transformer, export, etc.)
- `permissions`: Any permission not listed is denied by sandbox
- `requirements.minFrameworkVersion` must be ≤ all API versions used
- `dependencies[].versionRange`: SemVer range syntax (PEP 440 compatible)

