## 8. Security & Governance

### Plugin Audit Checklist

Before deploying a plugin to production:

- [ ] Manifest schema valid
- [ ] All required permissions declared
- [ ] No `eval()`, `Function()`, or dynamic code execution
- [ ] No network calls outside declared scope
- [ ] No file access outside `/tmp/plugin-cache`
- [ ] Dependencies pinned to exact versions
- [ ] Source code reviewed by security team
- [ ] Tests cover happy path + error cases
- [ ] Timeout assertions (no infinite loops)
- [ ] Sensitive config marked `sensitive: true`

### Permission Audit Trail

```typescript
// Log all permission checks
class AuditedSandbox extends SandboxExecutor {
  async executeHook(...) {
    const auditLog = [];

    const checkedPermission = (resource: string, action: string, allowed: boolean) => {
      auditLog.push({
        timestamp: new Date(),
        resource,
        action,
        allowed,
        pluginId: this.currentPluginId,
      });
    };

    // Write audit log to persistent storage
    await auditLogger.write(auditLog);
  }
}
```

### Malicious Plugin Mitigations

| Attack | Defense |
|--------|---------|
| Memory bomb | WorkerThread memory limit + GC |
| Fork bomb | `child_process` unavailable in sandbox |
| Network scanning | Network permission + scope restriction |
| Data exfiltration | Audit logging + scope restrictions |
| Privilege escalation | Sandboxed context, no OS access |
| Dependency confusion | Only npm packages in allowlist |

