## 8. Best Practices & Guidelines for Plugin Teams

### 8.1 Plugin Development Checklist

- [ ] Manifest includes all required fields
- [ ] Declared permissions match actual usage
- [ ] Entry point exports all declared capabilities
- [ ] Implements all required lifecycle hooks
- [ ] Health checks respond within 5 seconds
- [ ] No direct `process`, `fs`, or `require` (use injected APIs)
- [ ] State is properly serializable for hot reload
- [ ] Errors are caught and logged, not thrown to sandbox boundary
- [ ] Respects resource limits (memory, CPU, timeout)
- [ ] Includes integration tests with registry

### 8.2 Versioning Strategy

- Patch (1.0.0 → 1.0.1): Bug fixes, no API changes
- Minor (1.0.0 → 1.1.0): New capabilities, backward compatible
- Major (1.0.0 → 2.0.0): Breaking changes, may require API version update
- Deprecate APIs with 2 minor versions notice before removal

### 8.3 Upgrade Path

```typescript
// Old plugin (API v1.0)
export class MyPlugin implements ReportingPluginAPI_v1 {
  async initialize() { /* ... */ }
}

// Upgraded plugin (API v1.1) - backward compatible
export class MyPlugin implements ReportingPluginAPI_v1_1 {
  async initialize() { /* ... */ }
  async onHotReload(state) { /* ... */ }
}

// New major version (API v2.0) - breaking change
export class MyPlugin implements ReportingPluginAPI_v2 {
  async initialize() { /* ... */ }
  async execute(request) { /* new interface */ }
}
