## 7. Plugin Communication & Dependency Management

### 7.1 Inter-Plugin Communication

```typescript
// Plugins communicate through a pub/sub event system
interface PluginEventBus {
  // Publish event (only to this plugin's subscribers and core)
  emit(event: string, data: unknown): void;

  // Subscribe to events from other plugins
  on(event: string, handler: (data: unknown) => void): Disposable;

  // Subscribe once
  once(event: string): Promise<unknown>;
}

// Events are scoped to prevent accidental conflicts
// com.example.exporter.ready
// com.other.importer.loaded
// reporting-tool.report.created (core events)

// Example: Plugin A publishes, Plugin B consumes
// Plugin A (activate hook):
api.events.emit('com.example.exporter.ready', { version: '1.0' });

// Plugin B manifest:
