## 11. Security Considerations

### 11.1 Security Model

```typescript
// Plugin sandbox enforces:
// 1. No direct process access (no child_process module)
// 2. Filesystem access mediated and logging all operations
// 3. Network access via allowlist only
// 4. No access to other plugin memory
// 5. No access to host internal APIs
// 6. CPU/memory/timeout limits enforced
// 7. All IPC calls authenticated and authorized

// Security boundaries:
// - Each plugin runs in isolated Worker thread
// - Communication is message-based, not shared memory
// - Host can kill plugin at any time
// - Plugin cannot escape sandbox

// Threat model:
// - Plugin bugs causing crashes → isolated, doesn't crash host
// - Plugin DoS attempt → resource limits + timeout
// - Plugin accessing user data → sandbox prevents it
// - Plugin trying to compromise other plugins → isolated process
// - Plugin with malicious intent → permissions model stops exploitation
```

### 11.2 Dependency Security

```typescript
