### 1.2 Manifest Fields Reference

| Field | Type | Required | Purpose |
|-------|------|----------|---------|
| `apiVersion` | string | ✓ | Format: `plugin.reporting.io/v<N>`. Must match host's supported versions. |
| `kind` | string | ✓ | Always `"Plugin"` for this schema. |
| `metadata.name` | string | ✓ | Kebab-case, globally unique identifier. |
| `metadata.displayName` | string | ✓ | Human-readable name for UI. |
| `metadata.version` | string | ✓ | Semver (e.g., `1.2.3`). Plugins with same name but different versions can coexist. |
| `spec.entrypoint` | string | ✓ | Path to exported handler object (relative to manifest). |
| `spec.minCoreVersion` | string | ✓ | Minimum host version. Semver range. |
| `spec.maxCoreVersion` | string | ✗ | Maximum host version. Omit for "any newer version". Format: `"4.x"`, `"^4.0.0"`, or `"5.0.0"`. |
| `spec.dependencies` | object | ✗ | Map of `pluginName: semverRange`. Registry resolves before load. |
| `spec.capabilities` | object | ✗ | Declares what the plugin does; gates permission prompts and API access. |
| `spec.resources` | object | ✗ | Execution sandbox limits. Defaults: 512 MB, 10 concurrent, 60s timeout. |
| `spec.hooks` | object | ✗ | Lifecycle methods. Properties reference exported handler functions. |
| `spec.exports` | object | ✗ | What the plugin provides to the host and other plugins. |
| `spec.configuration` | object | ✗ | JSON Schema + UI Schema for user-editable settings. |

