## 4. Sandboxed Execution Boundary

### 4.1 Isolation Model

```
┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ Reporting Tool (Host)                              │
│                                                    │
│  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────┐  │
│  │ Plugin Sandbox 1 (pdf-export)               │  │
│  │                                             │  │
│  │ • Memory limit: 256 MB                      │  │
│  │ • Timeout: 30 seconds                       │  │
│  │ • FS access: /plugins/pdf-export only       │  │
│  │ • Network: Allow specific hosts (allowlist) │  │
│  │ • API: PluginAPI v1 (version-locked)       │  │
│  │                                             │  │
│  └─────────────────────────────────────────────┘  │
│                                                    │
│  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────┐  │
│  │ Plugin Sandbox 2 (data-connector)           │  │
│  │                                             │  │
│  │ • Memory limit: 512 MB                      │  │
│  │ • Timeout: 60 seconds                       │  │
│  │ • FS access: /plugins/data-connector only   │  │
│  │ • Database: Specific connection string      │  │
│  │ • API: PluginAPI v1 (version-locked)       │  │
│  │                                             │  │
│  └─────────────────────────────────────────────┘  │
│                                                    │
│ (Plugin crashes/hangs do NOT affect host or      │
│  other plugins; failures are isolated)            │
│                                                    │
└────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

### 4.2 Sandboxing Strategy (Node.js Implementation)

```typescript
interface SandboxConfig {
  pluginId: string;
  entrypointPath: string;
  memoryLimitMB: number;
  timeoutSeconds: number;
  fsRootPath: string; // plugins can only read/write here
  networkAllowlist?: string[]; // hosts allowed for fetch/http
  env: Record<string, string>; // safe subset of process.env
}

class PluginSandbox {
  // Spin up a Worker thread with isolated V8 heap
  private worker: Worker;

  async execute(
    handlerName: string,
    args: unknown[],
    context: PluginContext
  ): Promise<unknown> {
    return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
      const timeout = setTimeout(() => {
        this.worker.terminate();
        reject(new PluginError(
          'TIMEOUT',
          `Plugin execution exceeded ${this.config.timeoutSeconds}s`
        ));
      }, this.config.timeoutSeconds * 1000);

      this.worker.on('message', (result) => {
        clearTimeout(timeout);
        if (result.error) {
          reject(new PluginError(result.code, result.error));
        } else {
          resolve(result.data);
        }
      });

      this.worker.on('error', (error) => {
        clearTimeout(timeout);
        reject(error);
      });

      // Send execution request to worker
      this.worker.postMessage({
        handler: handlerName,
        args,
        context
      });
    });
  }
}

// Worker thread isolation:
// 1. Separate V8 heap → memory limit enforced by OS
// 2. Separate event loop → one plugin's blocking call doesn't block others
// 3. Require() interception → only allow safe modules (fs access proxied)
// 4. Network interception → validate against allowlist
// 5. Child process restriction → no spawn()
// 6. Eval restriction → no eval/Function/require() of untrusted code
```

### 4.3 Filesystem Sandboxing

```typescript
interface SandboxedFileSystem {
  // All paths validated against plugin's root directory

  async readFile(path: string): Promise<Buffer>;
  async writeFile(path: string, data: Buffer): Promise<void>;
  async listDirectory(path: string): Promise<string[]>;
  async deleteFile(path: string): Promise<void>;

  // Path resolution with ".." prevention
  resolvePath(input: string): string {
    const resolved = Path.resolve(this.rootPath, input);
    if (!resolved.startsWith(this.rootPath)) {
      throw new SecurityError('Path traversal detected');
    }
    return resolved;
  }
}

// Example: PDF plugin attempts directory traversal
const fs = context.fs;
await fs.readFile('../../secrets.env'); // Throws SecurityError
await fs.readFile('./config.json'); // ✓ Allowed
```

### 4.4 Resource Enforcement

```typescript
interface ResourceMonitor {
  // Tracked per plugin instance
  memoryUsageMB: number; // updated every 100ms
  executionTimeMs: number;
  activeRequests: number;

  enforce(config: ResourceLimits): void {
    if (this.memoryUsageMB > config.maxMemoryMB) {
      // Send kill signal to sandbox
      sandbox.terminate();
      throw new PluginError('MEMORY_LIMIT_EXCEEDED',
        `Plugin used ${this.memoryUsageMB}MB, limit ${config.maxMemoryMB}MB`);
    }

    if (this.activeRequests > config.maxConcurrency) {
      throw new PluginError('CONCURRENCY_LIMIT_EXCEEDED',
        `Too many concurrent operations`);
    }
  }
}
```

