## 7. Security Considerations

### 7.1 Plugin Trust Model

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ Plugin Trust Levels                                     │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│                                                         │
│ TRUSTED (digitally signed by vendor)                   │
│ • Full API access (within declared capabilities)       │
│ • Network access, database access allowed              │
│ • Can be updated automatically                         │
│ Example: Official PDF Export plugin from vendor        │
│                                                         │
│ SEMI-TRUSTED (from known organization, unsigned)       │
│ • API access limited to declared capabilities          │
│ • Network/DB access requires explicit approval         │
│ • Manual update approval required                      │
│ Example: PDF Export built by Team Analytics            │
│                                                         │
│ UNTRUSTED (unknown origin)                             │
│ • Sandboxed: minimal API, no network/DB                │
│ • User prompted before load                            │
│ • Manual update approval always required               │
│ Example: Third-party marketplace plugin                │
│                                                         │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

### 7.2 Capability Grants

Plugins declare capabilities; host controls access based on trust level.

```typescript
// Plugin requests database access (in manifest)
"capabilities": {
  "databaseAccess": true
}

// Host decision (configurable per trust level)
if (plugin.trustLevel === 'TRUSTED') {
  grantCapability('databaseAccess');
} else if (plugin.trustLevel === 'SEMI_TRUSTED') {
  // Prompt user on first access
  const approved = await promptUser(`Allow ${plugin.name} to access database?`);
  if (approved) grantCapability('databaseAccess');
} else {
  // UNTRUSTED: deny
  denyCapability('databaseAccess');
}

// At runtime, capability enforcement
if (plugin.capabilities.databaseAccess && plugin.grantedCapabilities.has('databaseAccess')) {
  return context.api.reports; // ✓ Allowed
} else {
  throw new PermissionError('Plugin not granted database access');
}
```

### 7.3 Sensitive Data Protection

```typescript
// Configuration schema marks fields as sensitive
"configuration": {
  "schema": {
    "apiKey": {
      "type": "string",
      "sensitive": true  // ← Encrypted at rest, masked in logs
    }
  }
}

// In plugin code:
const config = context.config; // {apiKey: "••••••••••"} (redacted in logs)

// Actual value passed to plugin in secure context (not logged)
const apiKey = config.apiKey; // "actual-key-value"

// In network calls:
try {
  await fetch('https://api.example.com', {
    headers: { 'Authorization': `Bearer ${apiKey}` }
  });
} catch (error) {
  // apiKey never appears in error message
  context.logger.error('API request failed: network error');
}
```

