## 3. Plugin Registry

The registry is the single source of truth for installed plugins, their metadata, and their runtime state.

### 3.1 Registry Responsibilities

```typescript
interface PluginRegistry {
  // Discovery & Metadata
  list(filter?: RegistryFilter): Promise<PluginMetadata[]>;
  get(pluginId: string): Promise<PluginMetadata | undefined>;
  search(query: string): Promise<PluginMetadata[]>;

  // Installation & Removal
  install(source: PluginSource): Promise<Installation>;
  uninstall(pluginId: string): Promise<void>;

  // Updates & Versioning
  checkUpdates(pluginId: string): Promise<UpdateInfo | null>;
  upgrade(pluginId: string, targetVersion: string): Promise<void>;

  // Runtime State
  getRuntime(pluginId: string): Promise<PluginRuntime>;
  setRuntime(pluginId: string, state: Partial<PluginRuntime>): Promise<void>;

  // Dependency Resolution
  resolveDependencies(pluginId: string): Promise<DependencyGraph>;
  validateCompatibility(pluginId: string, apiVersion: string): Promise<Compatibility>;
}

interface PluginMetadata {
  id: string;
  name: string;
  version: string;
  type: PluginType;
  minApiVersion: string;
  maxApiVersion: string;
  status: "installed" | "disabled" | "error";
  description: string;
  author: Author;
  capabilities: Capability[];
  dependencies: Dependency[];
  permissions: Permission[];
  checksum: string; // SHA-256 of dist for integrity
  installationPath: string;
  installedAt: ISO8601DateTime;
  lastUpdatedAt: ISO8601DateTime;
  nextUpgradeAvailableAt?: ISO8601DateTime;
}

interface PluginRuntime {
  pluginId: string;
  status: "idle" | "loading" | "active" | "unloading" | "failed";
  instance: PluginInstance | null;
  lastError?: PluginError;
  loadedAt?: ISO8601DateTime;
  unloadedAt?: ISO8601DateTime;
  resourceUsage: {
    memoryMb: number;
    cpuMs: number;
    activeRequests: number;
  };
  hooks: HookSubscription[];
}

type PluginSource =
  | { type: "package"; url: string; version?: string }
  | { type: "git"; url: string; ref?: string }
  | { type: "local"; path: string };
```

### 3.2 Registry Storage & Discovery

**Plugin Discovery Paths** (in order of precedence):

1. `/opt/reporting-tool/plugins/` - Core-bundled plugins (read-only)
2. `~/.reporting-tool/plugins/` - User-installed plugins
3. Environment: `REPORTING_PLUGIN_PATH` - Custom plugin directories
4. Registry: Central plugin repository (optional; curated third-party)

**Each plugin location contains**:
```
my-plugin/
├── plugin.json          (manifest, validated at install)
├── package.json         (npm metadata, if applicable)
├── dist/                (built/transpiled code)
│   ├── index.js
│   └── types.d.ts
├── node_modules/        (dependencies; bundled or managed)
├── .plugin-lockfile     (dependency versions locked at install)
└── .plugin-metadata     (runtime metadata: permissions, status)
```

**Registry State Storage** (durable):
