## 9. Security Considerations

### 9.1 Threat Model

| Threat | Mitigation |
|--------|-----------|
| Malicious plugin reads env secrets | Capability-based permission model; only grant needed env vars |
| Plugin DoS via infinite loop | CPU time limit + timeout enforcement |
| Plugin exhausts memory | Heap limit via process V8 options |
| Plugin exfiltrates data | Network permission restrictions to allowed hosts only |
| Plugin breaks out of sandbox | Run in separate process/worker; OS-level isolation |
| Supply-chain compromise of dependencies | Plugin manifest pins exact versions; checksums verified at install |
| Tampering with installed plugin | Checksum validated before every load |

### 9.2 Installation Security

```typescript
async installPlugin(source: PluginSource): Promise<void> {
  // 1. Download/fetch plugin
  const code = await this.download(source);

  // 2. Verify signature (if signed)
  if (code.signature) {
    await verifySignature(code, source.publicKey);
  }

  // 3. Parse manifest
  const manifest = await parseManifest(code.manifest);

  // 4. Validate manifest structure
  await validateManifest(manifest);

  // 5. Check API compatibility
  const hostVersion = getCurrentAPIVersion();
  if (!isCompatible(manifest.minApiVersion, hostVersion, manifest.maxApiVersion)) {
    throw new Error(
      `Plugin requires API ${manifest.minApiVersion}-${manifest.maxApiVersion}; ` +
      `host provides ${hostVersion}`
    );
  }

  // 6. Prompt admin for permission review
  const approved = await this.promptAdminApproval({
    pluginId: manifest.id,
    permissions: manifest.capabilities.permissions,
    description: manifest.description,
  });
  if (!approved) throw new Error("Installation cancelled");

  // 7. Extract & store
  const installPath = this.getInstallPath(manifest.id);
  await extract(code.archive, installPath);

  // 8. Compute checksum
  const checksum = await hashDirectory(installPath);

  // 9. Store metadata
  await this.persistInstallation({
    ...manifest,
    installationPath: installPath,
    checksum: checksum,
    approvedPermissions: approved.permissions,
    installedAt: new Date().toISOString(),
  });
}
```

