## 2. Plugin Registry & Discovery

### 2.1 Registry Architecture

The plugin registry is a centralized, immutable-by-default datastore that maintains plugin metadata, versions, and operational state.

```
registry/
├── manifests/           # Plugin metadata
├── versions/            # Version-indexed metadata
├── runtime-state/       # Loaded plugins, hooks, dependencies
└── audit-log/           # All registry modifications
```

### 2.2 Registry Interface

**Core Registry Operations:**

```typescript
interface IPluginRegistry {
  // Registration
  register(manifest: PluginManifest): Promise<RegistryToken>;
  unregister(pluginId: string, version?: string): Promise<void>;

  // Lookup
  get(pluginId: string, version?: semver): Promise<PluginMetadata | null>;
  list(filters?: RegistryFilter): Promise<PluginMetadata[]>;
  resolve(dependency: DependencySpec): Promise<PluginMetadata>;

  // Lifecycle
  setLoadState(pluginId: string, state: LoadState): Promise<void>;
  getLoadState(pluginId: string): Promise<LoadState>;

  // Validation
  validate(manifest: PluginManifest): Promise<ValidationResult>;
}

type LoadState = 'registered' | 'loaded' | 'active' | 'suspended' | 'failed' | 'unloaded';
```

