## 5. Sandboxed Execution Model

Plugins run in isolated V8 VM contexts (via vm2 or custom implementation) with:
- Controlled global scope (no eval, Function constructor)
- Capability-gated API access (permissions enforce what plugins can call)
- Resource limits (memory, CPU timeout, disk, network quotas)
- Network isolation (whitelist-only, no localhost)

```typescript
export class PluginSandbox {
  async load(entrypoint: string): Promise<PluginModule>;

  // Resource monitoring
  checkMemoryQuota(bytes: number): void;
  checkDiskQuota(bytes: number): void;
  checkNetworkQuota(url: string): void;

  // Cleanup
  async cleanup(): Promise<void>;
}

// Sandboxed globals: console, Promise, Error, setTimeout/clearTimeout only
// Sandboxed require: whitelisted modules from manifest.dependencies
// Sandboxed process: minimal env vars (NODE_ENV, PLUGIN_ID only)
