## 5. Sandboxed Execution Boundary

### 5.1 Isolation Strategy

Plugins execute in **namespace isolation** with **capability-based access control**:

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────┐
│         Plugin Process / Worker         │
│  (Restricted Node.js context)           │
├─────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ ✓ Access: Granted APIs & Capabilities   │
│ ✓ Access: Declared file paths           │
│ ✗ Access: process.env (undefined)       │
│ ✗ Access: require() (blocked)           │
│ ✗ Access: Network (unless permitted)    │
│ ✗ Access: process (blocked)             │
│ ✗ Access: Other plugins' state          │
└─────────────────────────────────────────┘
         ↑ Registry (IPC/boundary)
┌─────────────────────────────────────────┐
│      Core Reporting Tool Runtime        │
│      (Full access, trusted)             │
└─────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

### 5.2 Sandbox Initialization

```typescript
interface PluginSandbox {
  // Environment: plugin-specific, locked
  env: Record<string, string>           // Only declared env vars
  cwd: string                           // Isolated temp directory

  // Capabilities: granted by registry
  permissions: PermissionSet

  // Communication: via bridge only
  invoke(api: string, args: unknown): Promise<unknown>
  emit(event: string, data: unknown): void

  // State: isolated per plugin
  localStorage: Map<string, string>     // In-memory or persisted
}

class SandboxBridge {
  // Validate all cross-boundary calls
  async invoke<T>(
    plugin: Plugin,
    capability: string,
    args: unknown
  ): Promise<T> {
    // 1. Verify capability in manifest
    // 2. Validate args against input schema
    // 3. Check permissions
    // 4. Execute handler
    // 5. Validate output against schema
    // 6. Return result or throw PluginError
  }
}
```

### 5.3 Permission Model

```typescript
type PermissionAction = "read" | "write" | "execute" | "invoke"
type PermissionResource = 
  | `file://${string}`          // File system paths
  | `api://${string}`           // API endpoints
  | `plugin://${string}`        // Plugin-to-plugin calls
  | `env://${string}`           // Environment variables
  | `network://${string}`       // Network destinations

interface Permission {
  action: PermissionAction
  resource: PermissionResource
  conditions?: {
    maxSize?: number
    timeout?: number
    rateLimit?: number
  }
}

// Permission checking happens at the bridge:
class PermissionValidator {
  check(
    plugin: Plugin,
    action: PermissionAction,
    resource: PermissionResource
  ): boolean {
    const perm = plugin.manifest.permissions
      .find(p => p.action === action && p.resource === resource)

    return perm !== null
  }
}
```

### 5.4 Error Containment

```typescript
class PluginError extends Error {
  code: 
    | "LOAD_FAILED"
    | "UNLOAD_FAILED"
    | "INVOKE_FAILED"
    | "PERMISSION_DENIED"
    | "SCHEMA_VALIDATION_FAILED"
    | "DEPENDENCY_NOT_FOUND"
    | "TIMEOUT"
    | "CRASH"

  pluginId: string
  cause?: Error
  timestamp: Date
}

// Plugin crash does NOT affect registry:
try {
  await plugin.invoke("exporters/pdf", data)
} catch (err) {
  if (err instanceof PluginError && err.code === "CRASH") {
    registry.emit("pluginCrashed", {
      pluginId: err.pluginId,
      error: err.cause
