## 11. Deployment & Operations

### 11.1 Plugin Package Format

Plugins are distributed as:

```
plugin.tar.gz
├── manifest.json                   (schema: PluginManifest)
├── plugin.js                       (bundled, validated)
├── plugin.js.sha256                (integrity check)
└── PLUGIN_SIGNATURE.bin            (signed by plugin author)
```

### 11.2 Registry Startup

```typescript
async function initializeRegistry() {
  const registry = new PluginRegistry()

  // Load plugins from installation directory
  const pluginDir = process.env.PLUGIN_DIR || "/opt/plugins"
  const manifests = await findManifests(pluginDir)

  for (const manifest of manifests) {
    try {
      // Verify signature
      await verifySignature(manifest)

      // Load plugin
      await registry.register({
        manifest,
        code: await loadCode(manifest)
      })

      logger.info(`Loaded plugin: ${manifest.id}@${manifest.version}`)
    } catch (err) {
      logger.error(`Failed to load plugin: ${manifest.id}`, err)
      // Continue; other plugins unaffected
    }
  }

  return registry
}
```

