## **1. Plugin Manifest Schema** (YAML)

Each plugin declares its contract in `plugin-manifest.yml`:

```yaml
apiVersion: "plugins/v1"
kind: "Plugin"
metadata:
  id: "com.acme.sales-forecast"           # Globally unique, reverse DNS
  name: "Sales Forecast Reporter"
  version: "2.1.0"                        # Semantic versioning
  author: "ACME Analytics"
  description: "Generates sales forecasts using ML models"

spec:
  # API versioning for multi-version support
  compatibleApiVersions: ["2.0", "2.1"]
  minHostVersion: "5.0.0"

  # Entry points
  main: "./dist/index.js"
  uiMain: "./dist/ui.js"

  # Plugin dependencies
  dependencies:
    - id: "com.reporting.datasources"
      version: "^1.0.0"

  # Required capabilities (permission model)
  capabilities:
    - "datasource:read"
    - "report:write"
    - "schedule:create"
    - "network:http"
    - "storage:plugin-local"
    - "secrets:read"

  # Lifecycle hooks the plugin implements
  hooks:
    onLoad: true
    onUnload: true
    onReload: true

  # Resource constraints enforced
  resources:
    memory: "512Mi"
    timeout: "30s"
    diskQuota: "100Mi"

  # Configuration schema (JSON Schema)
  config:
    schema:
      type: "object"
      properties:
        apiKey:
          type: "string"
          secret: true
        refreshInterval:
          type: "integer"
          default: 3600
      required: ["apiKey"]

  # What this plugin exports for other plugins
  exports:
    - name: "ForecastModel"
      version: "1.0.0"

distribution:
  registry: true
  tags: ["forecasting", "ml", "sales"]
  packages:
    - os: "linux"
      arch: "x64"
      url: "https://releases.acme.com/forecast-v2.1.0-linux.tar.gz"
      sha256: "abc123def456..."
