## **5. Sandboxed Execution Boundary**

Each plugin runs in an isolated V8 context with:

✗ **No access to:**
- Node.js globals (`require`, `fs`, `child_process`, `net`)
- Global `console` (use injected `plugin.logger` instead)
- Environment variables (use `plugin.context.config`)
- Direct network or file I/O

✓ **Only access to:**
- The injected `plugin` API object
- Capabilities declared in manifest
- Its own isolated storage
- Declared secrets (read-only)

**Resource enforcement:**
- Memory limits (e.g., 512MB max)
- Timeout enforcement (default 30s per execution)
- CPU time limits
- Disk quota per plugin
- Private IP requests blocked (unless allowlisted)

