## 5. Sandboxed Execution Boundary

Plugins execute in isolated worker threads/processes to prevent resource starvation and malicious code impact.

### 5.1 Sandbox Architecture

```typescript
interface SandboxConfig {
  // Resource limits
  maxMemoryMb: number;        // Default: 256
  maxExecutionTimeMs: number; // Default: 30000
  maxConnections: number;     // Default: 10

  // Allowed APIs
  allowedGlobals: string[];   // e.g., ["URL", "fetch", "Math"]
  allowedModules: string[];   // e.g., ["lodash", "date-fns"]

  // Worker configuration
  requiresWorkerThread: boolean;
  workerMemoryLimitMb?: number;

  // Filesystem
  allowFileSystemAccess: boolean;
  allowedPaths?: string[];    // Whitelisted directories

  // Network
  allowNetworkAccess: boolean;
  allowedDomains?: string[];  // Whitelisted domains
}

interface SandboxRuntime {
  // Execute code with sandbox constraints
  execute<T>(
    code: string,
    args: Record<string, unknown>,
    config: SandboxConfig
  ): Promise<T>;

  // Health check
  healthCheck(): Promise<{
    memoryUsageMb: number;
    isResponsive: boolean;
  }>;

  // Graceful shutdown
  terminate(timeoutMs?: number): Promise<void>;
}
```

### 5.2 Execution Model

```typescript
class WorkerSandbox implements SandboxRuntime {
  private worker: Worker;
  private healthCheckInterval: NodeJS.Timer;

  constructor(config: SandboxConfig) {
    // Create worker thread with resource limits
    this.worker = new Worker('./sandbox-worker.js', {
      resourceLimits: {
        maxOldSpaceSize: config.maxMemoryMb,
      },
    });

    // Setup message handlers
    this.worker.on('message', (msg) => this.handleMessage(msg));
    this.worker.on('error', (err) => this.handleError(err));

    // Periodic health checks
    this.healthCheckInterval = setInterval(
      () => this.healthCheck(),
      5000
    );
  }

  async execute<T>(
    code: string,
    args: Record<string, unknown>,
    config: SandboxConfig
  ): Promise<T> {
    const timeoutId = setTimeout(() => {
      this.worker.terminate();
      throw new Error(`Sandbox execution timeout after ${config.maxExecutionTimeMs}ms`);
    }, config.maxExecutionTimeMs);

    return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
      this.worker.once('message', (result) => {
        clearTimeout(timeoutId);
        if (result.error) {
          reject(new Error(result.error));
        } else {
          resolve(result.data);
        }
      });

      this.worker.postMessage({
        type: 'execute',
        code,
        args,
        config,
      });
    });
  }
}
```

### 5.3 Sandbox Isolation Strategies

| Strategy | Use Case | Overhead |
|----------|----------|----------|
| **Worker Thread** | Long-running plugins, DOM access | Low (shared memory) |
| **Child Process** | Untrusted code, native modules | Medium (IPC overhead) |
| **V8 Isolate** | High throughput, CPU-bound code | Low-Medium |
| **Container** | Maximum isolation, deployment | High (full container) |

**Recommendation**: Use Worker Threads for most plugins. Escalate to Child Processes for plugins requesting `filesystem.write` or `os.exec` permissions.

