## 11. Deployment & Distribution

### 11.1 Plugin Registry

Plugins can be distributed via:

1. **Official Registry** (curated, signed)
   - Automatic updates
   - Vulnerability scanning
   - Version management

2. **Private Registry** (on-premise)
   - Internal plugins
   - Custom installations
   - No public distribution

3. **Direct Installation**
   - File-based plugins
   - Git repositories
   - Development environments

### 11.2 Deployment Process

```
┌─ Plugin Development (in plugin repo)
├─ npm run build
├─ npm run test
├─ npm run package
└─ Generate manifest.json + code archive

┌─ Plugin Registry
├─ Receive plugin.tar.gz
├─ Verify signature (or require review)
├─ Scan for vulnerabilities
├─ Extract manifest
├─ Publish to registry catalog
└─ Make available for installation

┌─ Reporting Tool (admin)
├─ Browse available plugins
├─ Request permissions
├─ Approve/deny
└─ Install to local plugin directory

┌─ Reporting Tool (runtime)
├─ Discover plugins from plugin directory
├─ Load manifests
├─ Resolve dependencies
├─ Load plugins in isolation
└─ Execute lifecycle hooks
```

