## Sandboxing & Execution

Plugins run in isolated worker processes with strict resource limits.

```
┌────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│           Host Process                          │
│  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────┐  │
│  │ Plugin Registry / RPC Broker             │  │
│  │ - Resource Governor                      │  │
│  │ - Memory quota enforcement (256MB each)  │  │
│  │ - CPU limits                             │  │
│  │ - Call timeout enforcement (30s)         │  │
│  │ - Concurrency limiting (100 max)         │  │
│  └──────────────────────────────────────────┘  │
└────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
         ↓              ↓              ↓
    ┌────────┐    ┌────────┐    ┌────────┐
    │Plugin A│    │Plugin B│    │Plugin C│
    │Worker  │    │Worker  │    │Worker  │
    │256MB   │    │256MB   │    │256MB   │
    │timeout │    │timeout │    │timeout │
    │30s     │    │30s     │    │30s     │
    └────────┘    └────────┘    └────────┘
```

**Key Constraints:**
- Plugins cannot access filesystem directly
- No network access except through Host API
- No environment variables except whitelisted
- Memory capped at 256MB per plugin
- Each method call must complete in ≤ 30 seconds
- Max 100 concurrent calls across all plugins

