## API Contract & Versioning

The plugin API is versioned to allow evolution without breaking existing plugins.

### API v1.0 (Stable)

```typescript
namespace PluginAPI_v1_0 {
  export interface HostAPI {
    version: "1.0";

    // Logging
    logger: {
      info(message: string, context?: Record<string, any>): void;
      warn(message: string, context?: Record<string, any>): void;
      error(message: string, context?: Record<string, any>): void;
    };

    // Configuration
    config: {
      get<T>(path: string, defaultValue?: T): T;
      onChange(path: string, listener: (newValue: unknown) => void): () => void;
    };

    // Storage (per-plugin isolated)
    storage: {
      get<T>(key: string): Promise<T | null>;
      set<T>(key: string, value: T): Promise<void>;
      delete(key: string): Promise<void>;
      list(pattern?: string): Promise<string[]>;
    };

    // Data access
    data: {
      query(source: string, sql: string, params?: Record<string, unknown>): Promise<QueryResult>;
      write(source: string, table: string, rows: Record<string, unknown>[]): Promise<{ rowsWritten: number }>;
    };

    // Reporting
    reports: {
      render(spec: ReportSpec): Promise<RenderedReport>;
      schedule(reportId: string, spec: ReportSpec, cron: string): Promise<void>;
    };

    // Plugin messaging
    messaging: {
      send(targetPluginId: string, method: string, params: unknown): Promise<unknown>;
    };
  }
}
```

### Versioning Rules

- **MAJOR**: Breaking changes (e.g., remove method, change signature)
- **MINOR**: Additive changes (e.g., new method, new optional param)
- **PATCH**: Bug fixes only

**Compatibility:**
- v1.0 plugins run on v1.0, v1.1, v1.2, etc.
- v1.1 plugins do NOT run on v1.0 (require newer features)
- v2.0 is incompatible with all v1.x plugins (migration required)

