## Sandboxed Execution

### Sandbox Model

Plugins execute in isolated contexts with restricted capabilities:

```typescript
interface SandboxEnvironment {
  // Module isolation
  createModuleContext(pluginId: string, manifest: PluginManifest): ModuleContext;

  // Capability enforcement
  grantCapability(pluginId: string, capability: string): void;
  revokeCapability(pluginId: string, capability: string): void;
  hasCapability(pluginId: string, capability: string): boolean;

  // Resource limits
  setMemoryLimit(pluginId: string, limitMb: number): void;
  setTimeoutLimit(pluginId: string, timeoutMs: number): void;

  // Network control
  restrictNetwork(pluginId: string, allowlist: string[]): void;

  // Filesystem isolation
  isolateFilesystem(pluginId: string, allowedPaths: string[]): void;
}

interface ModuleContext {
  pluginId: string;
  // Minimal globals - no access to:
  // - require() (except whitelisted modules)
  // - import.meta
  // - process (except .env whitelisted vars)
  // - global object

  // Only accessible:
  // - hostAPI (restricted interface)
  // - console (logging, limited)
  // - standard globals (Math, JSON, etc.)
  // - setTimeout/setInterval (with limits)
}

enum SandboxLevel {
  STRICT = "strict",      // Minimal access, tight restrictions
  MODERATE = "moderate",  // Balanced, production default
  PERMISSIVE = "permissive" // Trusting plugins, internal use
}

interface CapabilityToken {
  capability: string;
  pluginId: string;
  grantedAt: number;
  expiresAt?: number; // TTL-based revocation
  metadata?: Record<string, any>;
}
```

### Security Boundaries

**What plugins CANNOT do:**
- Access the filesystem outside designated temp/persistent directories
- Make network requests to unlisted domains
- Access other plugins' state or context
- Import node modules directly (only through hostAPI)
- Execute arbitrary code (eval, Function constructors blocked)
- Access process environment
- Exceed memory or execution time limits
- Call host-internal APIs

**What plugins CAN do:**
- Use granted capabilities via hostAPI
- Log via provided logger
- Store plugin-scoped state
- Use standard JavaScript builtins
- Make network requests to allowlisted domains
- Access temp storage if configured
- Receive config from host at load time

### Capability-Based Permissions

Each capability maps to specific API surface:

```typescript
const CAPABILITY_MAPPING: Record<string, string[]> = {
  "datasource:read": ["hostAPI.query.execute", "hostAPI.query.executeStream"],
  "datasource:write": ["hostAPI.datasource.create", "hostAPI.datasource.update"],
  "report:create": ["hostAPI.report.create"],
  "report:modify": ["hostAPI.report.update"],
  "report:delete": ["hostAPI.report.delete"],
  "render:execute": ["hostAPI.render.render", "hostAPI.render.renderAsync"],
  "auth:context": ["hostAPI.auth.getCurrentUser", "hostAPI.auth.getAuthContext"],
  "storage:temp": ["hostAPI.storage.temp.read", "hostAPI.storage.temp.write"],
  "storage:persistent": ["hostAPI.storage.persistent.*"],
  "network:http": ["globalFetch"],
  "system:logging": ["globalLogger"],
};
