## Security Model

Defense-in-depth approach to plugin security.

### Permission-Based Access Control

Each plugin declares required permissions in its manifest:

```json
{
  "permissions": {
    "required": [
      {
        "resource": "api:reports",
        "actions": ["read", "write"],
        "constraints": {
          "rateLimit": 100
        }
      },
      {
        "resource": "storage:plugin-data",
        "actions": ["read", "write"],
        "constraints": {
          "maxSize": 52428800
        }
      }
    ],
    "optional": [
      {
        "resource": "network:external",
        "actions": ["read"],
        "constraints": {
          "allowedDomains": ["example.com"]
        }
      }
    ]
  }
}
```

At deployment time, operators approve permissions:

```typescript
interface PermissionApproval {
  pluginId: string
  version: string
  approvedPermissions: Permission[]     // What to allow
  deniedPermissions: Permission[]       // What to deny
  approver: string                      // Who approved
  approverEmail: string
  timestamp: Date
  reason?: string
  expiresAt?: Date                      // Time-limited approval
}

// Persisted to audit log, enabling compliance reporting
```

### Code Signing & Integrity

Plugin code is verified before loading:

```typescript
interface SignedPlugin {
  manifest: PluginManifest
  code: string
  signature: string                     // HMAC-SHA256 of manifest+code
  publicKey: string                     // Publisher's key ID
  timestamp: Date
  attestation?: string                  // Optional: Build attestation
}

class CodeSignatureVerifier {
  async verify(plugin: SignedPlugin): Promise<boolean> {
    // 1. Find publisher's public key
    const publisher = this.trustedPublishers.get(plugin.publicKey)
    if (!publisher) {
      throw new Error(`Unknown publisher: ${plugin.publicKey}`)
    }

    // 2. Verify signature
    const expected = crypto
      .createHmac("sha256", publisher.secret)
      .update(plugin.manifest + plugin.code)
      .digest("hex")

    if (plugin.signature !== expected) {
      throw new Error("Code signature verification failed")
    }

    // 3. Check timestamp freshness (optional)
    if (Date.now() - plugin.timestamp.getTime() > 30 * 24 * 60 * 60 * 1000) {
      console.warn("Plugin signature is over 30 days old")
    }

    return true
  }
}
```

### Audit Logging

All security-relevant events are logged:

```typescript
interface AuditLogEntry {
  timestamp: Date
  eventType:
    | "plugin_loaded"
    | "plugin_unloaded"
    | "permission_granted"
    | "permission_denied"
    | "code_signature_failed"
    | "resource_limit_exceeded"
    | "error"

  pluginId: string
  version: string
  actor: string                 // User/system
  action: string
  details: Record<string, any>
  result: "success" | "failure"
  error?: string
  ip?: string
  userAgent?: string
}

class AuditLogger {
  async log(entry: AuditLogEntry): Promise<void> {
    // 1. Persist to append-only log (immutable)
    await this.logStore.append(entry)

    // 2. Send to monitoring/alerting
    this.monitoring.record(entry)

    // 3. Alert on anomalies
    if (entry.eventType === "code_signature_failed") {
      this.alerting.sendAlert({
        severity: "critical",
        message: `Plugin code signature verification failed for ${entry.pluginId}`,
        details: entry
      })
    }
  }

  getAuditTrail(
    pluginId?: string,
    since?: Date,
    limit?: number
  ): AuditLogEntry[] {
    // Query immutable log for compliance reporting
  }
}
