## Security Model

Defense-in-depth: isolation, permissions, code signing, auditing.

### Permission-Based Access Control

Plugins declare permissions in manifest; operators approve at deployment:

```json
{
  "permissions": {
    "required": [
      {
        "resource": "api:reports",
        "actions": ["read"],
        "constraints": { "rateLimit": 100 }
      }
    ],
    "optional": [
      {
        "resource": "network:external",
        "actions": ["read"],
        "constraints": { "allowedDomains": ["example.com"] }
      }
    ]
  }
}
```

### Code Signing

Plugin packages include HMAC signature. Verified before loading:

```
SignedPlugin {
  manifest: PluginManifest
  code: string
  signature: string                 // HMAC-SHA256
  publicKey: string                 // Publisher ID
}
```

### Audit Logging

All security-relevant events logged:

```typescript
interface AuditLogEntry {
  timestamp: Date
  eventType: "plugin_loaded" | "permission_granted" | "error" | ...
  pluginId: string
  version: string
  actor: string                     // User/system
  action: string
  result: "success" | "failure"
  details?: any
}
```

