## **Critical Design Decisions**

| Decision | Chosen | Why | Trade-off |
|----------|--------|-----|-----------|
| **Isolation default** | Tier 2 (VM context) | Balances security & performance | Some process-level protection gaps |
| **Permission model** | Declarative, whitelist | Explicit security posture, auditable | Plugins must declare upfront |
| **Dependency resolution** | DAG + topological sort | Deterministic, clear boundaries | No circular dependencies allowed |
| **API stability** | Semantic versioning + compatibility window | Clear expectations, gradual migration | Need to maintain multiple versions |
| **Hot reload** | Optional per-plugin | Doesn't force complexity on all plugins | Requires careful request draining |
| **Code integrity** | HMAC signing, verify before load | Prevents tampering, enables compliance | Requires publisher PKI infrastructure |
| **Error handling** | Severity-based (warning/error/fatal) | Operators customize recovery | More categorization complexity |

