## 4. Sandboxed API

### 4.1 API Surface

Plugins access the host ONLY through the PluginAPI. All access is:
- **Capability-gated:** onLoad fails if manifest lacks required capability
- **Permission-scoped:** network domains, storage namespaces, secret names validated
- **Resource-limited:** memory, storage, connections, and request timeouts enforced
- **Error-isolated:** plugin errors don't crash host; caught and tracked per-plugin

```typescript
interface PluginAPI {
  version: string;  // e.g., "2.1"

  // Data: read-only + filtered access
  data: {
    getReport(id: string): Promise<Report>;
    queryDatasources(filter: any): Promise<Datasource[]>;
    getDatasourceData(id: string, params: any): Promise<QueryResult>;
    getCachedData(key: string): Promise<any>;
    setCachedData(key: string, value: any, ttl?: number): Promise<void>;
  };

  // Configuration: schema-validated
  config: {
    get<T = any>(key: string): T | undefined;
    set<T = any>(key: string, value: T): Promise<void>;
    getSchema(): JSONSchema;
    validate(config: any): ValidationResult;
  };

  // Execution: async, timeout-enforced
  execute: {
    query(sql: string, params?: any[]): Promise<QueryResult>;
    transform(data: any, fn: string): Promise<any>;
    schedule(name: string, cron: string, handler: () => Promise<void>): Promise<JobHandle>;
  };

  // Events: plugin-namespaced pub/sub
  events: {
    on(name: string, handler: (data: any) => void): void;
    off(name: string): void;
    emit(name: string, data: any): void;
  };

  // Network: domain-restricted
  network: {
    fetch(url: string, opts?: RequestInit): Promise<Response>;
    openWebSocket(url: string): Promise<WebSocketHandle>;
  };

  // Storage: namespaced, quota-enforced
  storage: {
    get(key: string): Promise<any>;
    set(key: string, value: any): Promise<void>;
    delete(key: string): Promise<void>;
    list(pattern: string): Promise<string[]>;
    getQuota(): Promise<{ used: number; limit: number }>;
  };

  // Secrets: declared in manifest
  secrets: {
    get(name: string): Promise<string | undefined>;
  };

  // Logging: captured + indexed
  logger: {
    debug(msg: string, data?: any): void;
    info(msg: string, data?: any): void;
    warn(msg: string, data?: any): void;
    error(msg: string, data?: any): void;
  };

  // Metrics: emitted to host
  metrics: {
    counter(name: string, value: number, tags?: Record<string, string>): void;
    gauge(name: string, value: number, tags?: Record<string, string>): void;
    histogram(name: string, value: number, tags?: Record<string, string>): void;
  };

  // Plugin metadata
  self: {
    id: string;
    version: string;
    manifest: PluginManifest;
    config: PluginConfig;
  };
}
```

### 4.2 Implementation Details

Each API method checks capabilities, validates permissions, enforces timeouts, and emits metrics. Plugins cannot access:
- Host internals or other plugins' instances
- File system (except via storage API with namespaced keys)
- Environment variables (except via secrets API with declared names)
- Network destinations outside allowed domains
- Resources beyond declared limits

