## 🎯 Plugin Manifest Schema

Every plugin defines capabilities and requirements:

```yaml
id: "@vendor/plugin-name"              # Reverse DNS format
version: "1.0.0"                       # Semantic versioning
apiVersion: "1.2"                      # API contract version
type: "reporter"                       # Plugin type

# Dependencies with semver ranges
dependencies:
  "@vendor/datasource": "^1.0.0"
optionalDependencies:
  "@vendor/formatter": "*"

# Capabilities with justification
capabilities:
  - name: "database.read"
    level: "medium"                    # low, medium, high, critical
    justification: "Read sales data"

# Fine-grained permissions
requiredPermissions:
  - id: "db-read"
    resource: "database"
    action: "read"
    scope: "/reports/**"               # Wildcard scoping

# Configuration schema
configSchema: {...}                    # JSON Schema
configDefaults:
  outputFormat: "pdf"

# Lifecycle hooks
hooks:
  onLoad: "initializePlugin"
  onEnable: "startServices"
  onConfigChange: "applyConfig"
```

