## API Reference

### PluginContext

Every plugin receives a context object with access to the host application:

```typescript
interface PluginContext {
  manifest: PluginManifest;      // Your manifest
  logger: PluginLogger;           // Logging interface
  api: ReportingAPI;              // Host API
  config: Record<string, unknown>;// Configuration
  runtime: PluginRuntime;         // Runtime metadata
}
```

#### logger

```typescript
context.logger.debug(message: string, data?: unknown): void
context.logger.info(message: string, data?: unknown): void
context.logger.warn(message: string, data?: unknown): void
context.logger.error(message: string, error?: Error): void
```

#### api.reports

```typescript
// List reports with filtering and pagination
const reports = await context.api.reports.list({
  limit: 50,
  offset: 0,
  filter: { status: 'published', format: 'pdf' },
  sort: [{ field: 'createdAt', order: 'desc' }]
});

// Get single report by ID
const report = await context.api.reports.get('report-123');

// Create new report
const newReport = await context.api.reports.create({
  title: 'My Report',
  format: 'pdf',
  status: 'draft',
  createdBy: 'system',
  data: { /* your data */ }
});

// Update report
const updated = await context.api.reports.update('report-123', {
  status: 'published',
  data: { /* updated data */ }
});

// Delete report
await context.api.reports.delete('report-123');

// Export to format
const blob = await context.api.reports.export('report-123', 'pdf');
```

#### api.config

```typescript
// Get configuration value
const value = await context.api.config.get('setting-key');

// Set configuration value
await context.api.config.set('setting-key', 'value');
```

#### api.events

```typescript
// Subscribe to events
const unsubscribe = context.api.events.on('report:published', (data) => {
  console.log('Report published:', data);
});

// Later: unsubscribe
unsubscribe();

// Emit custom events
await context.api.events.emit('my-plugin:action', {
  action: 'something',
  timestamp: new Date().toISOString()
});
```

### Lifecycle Hooks

#### onLoad

Called when plugin is loaded (required):

```typescript
export const onLoad = async (context: PluginContext) => {
  context.logger.info('Loading plugin');

  // Initialize resources
  await initializeDatabase();
  await loadConfiguration();

  context.logger.info('Plugin ready');
};
```

**Guarantees**:
- Runs once at load time
- Must complete before plugin is marked as loaded
- If throws, plugin enters error state
- Access to full API

#### onBeforeUnload

Called before unload (cleanup phase):

```typescript
export const onBeforeUnload = async (context: PluginContext) => {
  context.logger.info('Starting shutdown');
  // Flush pending work, save state
  await flushPendingRequests();
};
```

#### onUnload

Called when plugin unloads:

```typescript
export const onUnload = async (context: PluginContext) => {
  context.logger.info('Unloading plugin');
  // Release resources
  await closeDatabase();
  await closeConnections();
};
```

#### onReload

Called when plugin reloads (development):

```typescript
export const onReload = async (context: PluginContext) => {
  context.logger.info('Reloading plugin');
  // Clear caches, reload configuration
};
```

#### onError

Called when system error occurs (observe, don't throw):

```typescript
export const onError = async (context: PluginContext, error: any) => {
  context.logger.error('System error', error);
  // Send metrics, alert, etc.
};
```

#### onReportGenerated

Called after report is created (event hook):

```typescript
export const onReportGenerated = async (context: PluginContext, report: Report) => {
  // Don't throw - this is fire-and-forget
  try {
    context.logger.info('New report', {id: report.id, title: report.title});
    // Process report
  } catch (error) {
    context.logger.error('Failed to process report', error);
  }
};
```

#### onReportDeleted

Called after report is deleted:

```typescript
export const onReportDeleted = async (context: PluginContext, reportId: string) => {
  context.logger.info('Report deleted', {id: reportId});
  // Cleanup any plugin data for this report
};
```

## Permissions

Declare permissions your plugin needs in `plugin.json`:

```json
{
  "permissions": [
    "read:reports",      // List/get reports
    "write:reports",     // Create/update reports
    "delete:reports",    // Delete reports
    "execute:scripts",   // Run custom code
    "access:network",    // HTTP requests
    "read:filesystem",   // Read files
    "write:filesystem",  // Write files
    "read:secrets"       // Access config/secrets
  ]
}
```

**Access Control**: If a permission isn't declared, API calls using it throw an error.

```typescript
// Will fail if "write:reports" not declared
try {
  await context.api.reports.create({...});
} catch (error) {
  console.error('Permission denied:', error.code); // 'PERMISSION_DENIED'
}
```

## Configuration

Pass configuration to plugins at load time:

```typescript
const manager = new PluginManager(registry, {
  pluginDirs: ['/path/to/plugins'],
  sandboxConfig: {
    level: 'moderate',
    allowedPermissions: ['read:reports', 'write:reports'],
    memoryLimitMb: 256
  }
});

// Plugins access via context.config
export const onLoad = async (context: PluginContext) => {
  const dir = context.config.templateDir;
  const timeout = (context.config.timeout as number) || 5000;
};
```

## Error Handling

### Plugin Loading Errors

```typescript
try {
  await manager.loadPlugin('com.company.my-plugin');
} catch (error) {
  if (error.code === 'API_INCOMPATIBLE') {
    console.error('Plugin requires newer API version');
  } else if (error.code === 'DEPENDENCY_UNMET') {
    console.error('Missing dependencies:', error.details.missing);
  } else if (error.code === 'HOOK_ERROR') {
    console.error('Hook failed:', error);
  }
}
```

### API Errors

```typescript
export const onLoad = async (context: PluginContext) => {
  try {
    const reports = await context.api.reports.list();
  } catch (error) {
    if (error.code === 'PERMISSION_DENIED') {
      context.logger.error('Need read:reports permission');
    } else {
      context.logger.error('API call failed', error);
    }
  }
};
```

### Hook Errors

Errors in event hooks should be caught to not crash the system:

```typescript
export const onReportGenerated = async (context: PluginContext, report: Report) => {
  try {
    // Do work
  } catch (error) {
    // Log but don't throw
    context.logger.error('Failed to process report', error);
  }
};
```

## Dependencies

Plugins can depend on other plugins:

```json
{
  "dependencies": [
    {
      "id": "com.company.base-reporting",
      "version": "^1.0.0"
    }
  ]
}
```

Semver ranges supported:
- `"1.0.0"` - Exact version
- `"^1.0.0"` - Compatible with 1.x (>=1.0.0 <2.0.0)
- `"~1.2.0"` - Compatible with 1.2.x (>=1.2.0 <1.3.0)
- `">=1.0.0"` - Any version >= 1.0.0
- `"*"` - Any version

