## Best Practices

### 1. Declare Minimal Permissions

Only request permissions you actually need:

```json
{
  "permissions": ["read:reports"]
}
```

### 2. Handle Missing Permissions Gracefully

```typescript
export const onLoad = async (context: PluginContext) => {
  try {
    // Try to use permission
    await context.api.reports.create({...});
  } catch (error) {
    if (error.code === 'PERMISSION_DENIED') {
      context.logger.warn('Feature requires write:reports permission');
      // Disable this feature
    } else {
      throw error;
    }
  }
};
```

### 3. Don't Block in Event Hooks

Event hooks should complete quickly:

```typescript
export const onReportGenerated = async (context: PluginContext, report: Report) => {
  // Queue work to be processed async, don't await long operations
  processReportAsync(report).catch(err => {
    context.logger.error('Async processing failed', err);
  });
};
```

### 4. Clean Up in Lifecycle Hooks

```typescript
let intervalHandle: NodeJS.Timeout;

export const onLoad = async (context: PluginContext) => {
  intervalHandle = setInterval(() => {
    // Do work
  }, 5000);
};

export const onBeforeUnload = async (context: PluginContext) => {
  clearInterval(intervalHandle);
};
```

### 5. Use Semantic Versioning

Follow semver for your plugin:
- MAJOR: Breaking API changes
- MINOR: New features (backwards compatible)
- PATCH: Bug fixes

### 6. Document Your Plugin

```json
{
  "name": "My Plugin",
  "description": "What this plugin does and how to use it",
  "metadata": {
    "category": "export",
    "tags": ["pdf", "export"],
    "documentation": "https://docs.example.com/my-plugin"
  }
}
```

