### Manifest Schema Breakdown

| Section | Purpose |
|---------|---------|
| **Core Metadata** | id, name, version, author, license — uniquely identify plugin |
| **API Contract** | apiVersion — declares compatible host versions |
| **Entry Point** | main — where host loads plugin code from |
| **Capabilities** | Fine-grained permissions the plugin claims |
| **Dependencies** | Other plugins this plugin requires |
| **Resources** | Memory/CPU/disk limits and timeout expectations |
| **Hooks** | Which lifecycle events the plugin handles |
| **Configuration** | JSON Schema + UI definition for admin settings |
| **Extensions** | What new report types, transformations, connectors plugin provides |
| **Exports** | Public API surfaces available to other plugins/host |
| **Permissions** | Network, filesystem, environment variable access |
| **Metadata** | Platform support, deprecation info, breaking change timeline |
| **Telemetry** | Events and metrics the plugin emits |

