## Security Model

### Threat Model

| Threat | Mitigation |
|--------|-----------|
| Plugin reads unauthorized files | Filesystem capability model with path allowlist |
| Plugin makes unauthorized network calls | Network capability model with URL allowlist |
| Plugin accesses another plugin's memory | Process/thread isolation boundary |
| Plugin DoS through infinite loops | Timeout enforcement at sandbox level |
| Plugin DoS through memory exhaustion | Memory limits with automatic termination |
| Plugin steals credentials | Environment variable allowlist (manifest declares needs) |
| Plugin compromises core reporting logic | Capability-based sandboxing restricts API access |
| Malicious plugin manifest | Manifest validation + schema enforcement |

### Security Checklist

```typescript
interface SecurityPolicy {
  // Code signing
  enableCodeSigning: boolean;
  trustedSigners: string[]; // Public keys

  // Manifest validation
  validateManifestSchema: boolean;
  maxManifestSize: number; // Bytes

  // Capability enforcement
  capabilityModel: "strict" | "permissive"; // strict = deny-all by default
  auditCapabilityViolations: boolean;

  // Sandbox configuration
  isolationLevel: "vm" | "thread" | "process";
  enforceMemoryLimits: boolean;
  enforceCPULimits: boolean;
  enforceFileSystemBoundary: boolean;
  enforceNetworkBoundary: boolean;

  // Audit logging
  auditAllCapabilityChecks: boolean;
  auditAllNetworkAccess: boolean;
  auditAllFileSystemAccess: boolean;
  retentionDays: number;

  // Rate limiting
  enableRateLimiting: boolean;
  requestsPerSecond: number;

  // Supply chain security
  enableDependencyScanning: boolean;
  allowedPackageSources: string[];

  // Monitoring
  enableHealthMonitoring: boolean;
  healthCheckIntervalSeconds: number;
  unhealthyActionOnFailure: "disable" | "alert" | "none";
}
