## 4. Lifecycle Management

### 4.1 Plugin Lifecycle State Machine

```
                  ┌────────────────┐
                  │  NOT_INSTALLED │
                  └────────┬────────┘
                           │ install()
                           ▼
                  ┌────────────────┐
                  │   INSTALLED    │
                  └────────┬────────┘
                           │ load()
                           ▼
                  ┌────────────────┐
                  │    LOADING     │ ◄─┐ (retry on failure)
                  └────────┬────────┘   │
                           │            │
                    (success or timeout)│
                           ▼            │
        ┌──────────────────────────────┘
        │
        ▼
┌───────────────────┐         
│  LOADED (error)   │ ◄─────────────┐
└───────────────────┘              │
        ▲                          │
        │ (recovery attempt)       │
        │                          │
        ▼                          │
┌───────────────────┐     ┌────────────────┐
│   LOADED (ok)     │────►│    ENABLING    │
└────────┬──────────┘     └────────┬────────┘
         │                         │
         │  enable()               │ enable()
         │                         ▼
         │                ┌────────────────┐
         │                │   ENABLED      │
         │                └────────┬────────┘
         │                         │
         │                disable()│
         │                         ▼
         │                ┌────────────────┐
         │                │   DISABLING    │
         │                └────────┬────────┘
         │                         │
         │                         ▼
         └────────────────────────────────┐
                                          │
                                ┌─────────▼──────┐
                                │    DISABLED    │
                                └─────────┬──────┘
                                          │
                                  unload()│
                                          ▼
                                ┌─────────────────┐
                                │   UNLOADING     │
                                └────────┬────────┘
                                         │
                                         ▼
                                ┌─────────────────┐
                                │  NOT_LOADED     │
                                └─────────────────┘
```

### 4.2 Lifecycle Hooks

Each transition triggers hooks in the plugin that must complete within a timeout.

```typescript
interface PluginLifecycle {
  // Called when plugin is loaded into memory
  onLoad(context: PluginContext): Promise<void>;

  // Called when plugin transitions from LOADED to ENABLED
  onEnable(context: PluginContext): Promise<void>;

  // Called when plugin transitions from ENABLED to DISABLED
  onDisable(context: PluginContext): Promise<void>;

  // Called before plugin is unloaded (cleanup)
  onUnload(context: PluginContext): Promise<void>;

  // Called when reload is triggered (full restart)
  onReload(context: PluginContext): Promise<void>;

  // Called when error occurs at any stage
  onError(error: PluginError): Promise<void>;
}

interface PluginContext {
  pluginId: string;
  version: string;
  config: Record<string, unknown>;
  logger: Logger;
  store: ConfigurationStore;
  emit: EventEmitter;
  api: HostAPI; // Controlled access to host capabilities
}
```

### 4.3 Lifecycle Sequence: Plugin Load

```
User initiates: loadPlugin("my-plugin", "1.0.0")
                |
                ▼
        Validate manifest
                |
                ├─► (Invalid) ──► Emit error, return
                |
                ▼ (Valid)
        Resolve dependencies
                |
                ├─► (Unmet) ──► Emit warning, attempt to load dependencies
                |
                ▼ (Resolved)
        Create isolation sandbox
                |
                ▼
        Inject PluginContext
                |
                ▼
        Transition state: INSTALLED → LOADING
                |
                ▼
        Call plugin.onLoad(context) [timeout: manifest.spec.hooks.load.timeout]
                |
                ├─► (Success within timeout) ──► Transition: LOADING → LOADED
                |
                ├─► (Timeout) ──► Terminate sandbox, Transition: LOADING → LOADED (error)
                |
                ▼ (Exception)
        Emit error event, Transition: LOADING → LOADED (error)
                |
                ▼
        Return PluginDescriptor
```

### 4.4 Reload Strategy

Reload allows updating a plugin without full restart:

```typescript
async function reloadPlugin(pluginId: string, newConfig?: Record<string, unknown>) {
  const plugin = registry.get(pluginId);
  const wasEnabled = plugin.status === "ENABLED";

  // Step 1: Disable if enabled
  if (wasEnabled) {
    await plugin.onDisable(context);
  }

  // Step 2: Unload
  await plugin.onUnload(context);

  // Step 3: Reload manifest (detect version changes)
  const newManifest = await loadManifest(plugin.installPath);

  // Step 4: Update config
  if (newConfig) {
    validateConfig(newConfig, newManifest.spec.configuration.schema);
    plugin.config = newConfig;
  }

  // Step 5: Load fresh
  await plugin.onLoad(context);

  // Step 6: Re-enable if was enabled
  if (wasEnabled) {
    await plugin.onEnable(context);
  }

  return plugin;
}
```

