## 6. Versioned API Contract

### 6.1 API Versioning Strategy

We use **explicit versioning with co-existence** rather than breaking changes:

```typescript
namespace HostAPIv1 {
  interface Reports {
    read(reportId: string): Promise<Report>;
  }
}

namespace HostAPIv2 {
  interface Reports {
    read(reportId: string, options?: ReadOptions): Promise<Report>;
    readBatch(ids: string[]): Promise<Report[]>;
  }
}
```

**Compatibility Matrix:**

| Host Version | Supports API | Deprecates |
|--------------|--------------|-----------|
| 1.0.0 | v1 | - |
| 1.5.0 | v1, v2-beta | - |
| 2.0.0 | v1, v2 | - |
| 2.3.0 | v1*, v2, v3 | v1 (ends in 3.0.0) |
| 3.0.0 | v2, v3 | - |

### 6.2 Semantic Versioning Rules

```
MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH-PRERELEASE+BUILD

MAJOR: Breaking API changes, removed capabilities
MINOR: New capabilities, backward-compatible additions
PATCH: Bug fixes, performance improvements
```

### 6.3 Version Constraints in Dependencies

```json
{
  "spec": {
    "dependencies": {
      "plugins": [
        { "name": "base-reporting", "version": ">=1.0.0 <2.0.0" },
        { "name": "auth-plugin", "version": "1.5.x || 2.x" },
        { "name": "optional-plugin", "version": ">=1.0.0", "optional": true }
      ]
    },
    "compatibility": {
      "hostVersion": ">=1.0.0 <3.0.0",
      "apiVersion": ">=v1 <v3"
    }
  }
}
```

### 6.4 Deprecation Path

```typescript
interface DeprecationNotice {
  feature: string;
  removedInVersion: string;
  replacement?: string;
  alternative?: string;
  timeline: {
    deprecated: DateTime;
    supported: { from: DateTime; to: DateTime };
    removed: DateTime;
  };
}
```

**Process:**
1. Announce deprecation (3-month notice minimum)
2. Log warnings when deprecated feature used
3. Update documentation with migration guide
4. Continue supporting with compatibility shim
5. Remove in next MAJOR version

