## 11. Key Sequence Flows

### 11.1 Plugin Load Sequence

```
User: loadPlugin("team-acme:report-exporter", "2.1.0")
    ↓
1. Validate manifest
   ├─ Schema check
   ├─ Required fields
   └─ Environment compatibility
    ↓
2. Resolve dependencies
   ├─ Check all plugins in graph
   ├─ Validate versions
   └─ Detect circular dependencies
    ↓
3. Security check
   ├─ Verify code signature
   ├─ Check permissions
   └─ Apply security policies
    ↓
4. Initialize sandbox
   ├─ Allocate worker thread or process
   ├─ Set memory/CPU limits
   └─ Setup permission boundary
    ↓
5. Load code
   ├─ Require module
   ├─ Inject PluginContext
   └─ Setup logging
    ↓
6. Transition: LOADING → LOADED
    ↓
7. Execute onLoad() hook
   ├─ Plugin initialization logic
   ├─ Timeout after manifest.spec.hooks.load.timeout
   └─ Rollback on error
    ↓
8. Register subscriptions
   ├─ Setup event handlers
   └─ Setup RPC endpoints
    ↓
Success: Plugin LOADED, ready to enable
```

### 11.2 Plugin Reload Sequence

```
User: reloadPlugin("team-acme:report-exporter")
    ↓
1. If ENABLED → Disable
   ├─ Transition: ENABLED → DISABLING
   ├─ Execute onDisable() hook
   └─ Transition: DISABLING → DISABLED
    ↓
2. Unload
   ├─ Transition: DISABLED → UNLOADING
   ├─ Execute onUnload() hook
   ├─ Persist state
   └─ Transition: UNLOADING → UNINSTALLED
    ↓
3. Reload manifest (detect version changes)
    ↓
4. [REPEAT: Plugin Load Sequence]
    ↓
Success: Plugin reloaded and optionally re-enabled
```

### 11.3 Error Recovery

```
Runtime: Plugin crashes during execution
    ↓
1. Catch exception
   ├─ Capture stack trace
   ├─ Record correlation ID
   └─ Terminate sandbox
    ↓
2. Log error with full context
    ↓
3. Transition: ENABLED → ERROR
    ↓
4. Emit "plugin:error" event
    ↓
5. Recovery options:
   a) Auto-recovery (if timeout, transient error):
      ├─ Wait 5 seconds
      ├─ Attempt reload
      ├─ Resume if successful
      └─ Quarantine if fails 3x

   b) Manual recovery:
      ├─ Admin notified
      └─ Admin runs: pluginManager.recover(pluginId)
    ↓
Success or escalation to quarantine
```

