## 14. Design Decisions

| Decision | Choice | Rationale | Trade-off |
|----------|--------|-----------|-----------|
| Isolation | Worker Threads (default) | Fast IPC, lower overhead | Process isolation unavailable by default |
| Versioning | Semantic versioning + bridges | Clear contracts, prevents lock-in | Compatibility code maintenance |
| State | Distributed eventual consistency | Prevents deadlocks, scales | Possible temporary inconsistency |
| Permissions | Explicit allowlist (deny-by-default) | Security-first | Requires explicit capability requests |
| Error recovery | Exponential backoff + quarantine | Prevents cascades | Some requests fail fast initially |
| Manifest validation | Strict schema at load time | Catches issues early | Longer startup time |

---

## 15. Security Model Summary

- **Execution Isolation:** Worker threads with separate V8 isolates, message passing only
- **Permission Model:** Capability-based (fine-grained), not role-based
- **Network Security:** Allowlist with domain/port restrictions
- **Data Protection:** Tenant-scoped access, encryption at rest
- **Audit Trail:** All operations logged with full context
- **Secret Management:** Encrypted config storage, no hardcoded secrets
- **Dependency Security:** Pinned versions, integrity checking, vulnerability scanning

