## 3. Plugin Registry

The registry manages plugin discovery, version tracking, dependency resolution, and lifecycle state.

### 3.1 Registry Interface

```typescript
interface PluginRegistry {
  // Discovery
  discover(): Promise<PluginMetadata[]>;
  getPlugin(id: string): RegistryEntry | undefined;
  getAllPlugins(): PluginMetadata[];

  // Dependency resolution
  getLoadOrder(): string[]; // Topological sort
  resolveDependencies(pluginId: string): {
    satisfied: boolean;
    missing: string[];
    conflicts: string[];
  };

  // State management
  setEnabled(id: string, enabled: boolean): void;
  getStatus(id: string): 'unloaded' | 'loading' | 'loaded' | 'error';
  setStatus(id: string, status: string, error?: Error): void;
  clearError(id: string): void;

  // Event subscriptions
  on(event: string, callback: Function): void;
  off(event: string, callback: Function): void;
}

interface PluginMetadata {
  id: string;
  name: string;
  version: string;
  manifest: PluginManifest;
  path: string;
  enabled: boolean;
  loadedAt?: Date;
  status: 'unloaded' | 'loading' | 'loaded' | 'error';
  error?: Error;
}

interface RegistryEntry {
  metadata: PluginMetadata;
  dependencies: PluginDependency[];
  dependents: string[]; // plugins that depend on this
  instance?: PluginInstance;
}
```

### 3.2 Key Registry Operations

**Discover plugins:**
```typescript
const registry = new PluginRegistry({ searchPaths: ['./plugins'] });
const discovered = await registry.discover();
// Returns all plugins found in searchPaths
```

**Check dependencies:**
```typescript
const resolution = registry.resolveDependencies('com.example.plugin');
if (!resolution.satisfied) {
  console.log('Missing:', resolution.missing);
  console.log('Version conflicts:', resolution.conflicts);
}
```

**Get load order:**
```typescript
const order = registry.getLoadOrder();
// Returns [pluginA, pluginB, pluginC, ...]
// Dependencies always load before dependents
```

