## 4. Lifecycle Management

### 4.1 Plugin State Machine

```
         load()
    ┌──────────────┐
    │              ▼
[unloaded] ──► [loading] ──────┐
                  │             │
                  ├─ error ────► [error] ◄──┐
                  │             ▲           │
                  ▼             │ retry     │
              [loaded] ─────────┼──────────┐│
                  ▲             │          ││
                  │ reload()    │          ││
              [reloading] ◄─────┴──────────┘│
                  │                        │
                  ├─ error ────────────────┘
                  ▼
              [loaded]

         unload()
    ┌──────────────┐
    │              ▼
[loaded] ──► [unloading] ──► [unloaded]
    │           │
    └─ error ───► [error]
```

### 4.2 Lifecycle Manager Interface

```typescript
interface LifecycleManager {
  // Load operations
  load(pluginId: string): Promise<PluginInstance>;
  loadAll(): Promise<{ loaded: string[]; failed: Array<{ id: string; error: Error }> }>;

  // Unload operations
  unload(pluginId: string): Promise<void>;
  unloadAll(): Promise<{ unloaded: string[]; errors: Array<{ id: string; error: Error }> }>;

  // Hot reload
  reload(pluginId: string): Promise<PluginInstance>;

  // Query
  getInstance(pluginId: string): PluginInstance | undefined;
  getAllInstances(): PluginInstance[];

  // Events
  on(event: string, callback: Function): void;
}

interface PluginInstance {
  id: string;
  version: string;
  exports: PluginExports;
  context: PluginContext;
  state: PluginState;
  hooks: Map<string, PluginHook[]>;
}

interface PluginExports {
  onLoad?(): Promise<void>;
  onUnload?(): Promise<void>;
  onReload?(): Promise<void>;
  configure?(config: any): Promise<void>;
  hooks?: Record<string, PluginHook>;
}

interface PluginContext {
  pluginId: string;
  version: string;
  api: CoreAPI; // See section 7
  storage: PluginStorage;
  logger: Logger;
  config: any;
}

interface PluginState {
  data: Map<string, any>;
  persistent: boolean;
}
```

### 4.3 Load Sequence

```typescript
async load(pluginId: string): Promise<PluginInstance> {
  1. Verify dependencies are loaded
     ├─ Check manifest.spec.dependencies
     ├─ Load missing dependencies first
     └─ Detect circular dependencies

  2. Create sandbox
     ├─ Allocate VM context
     ├─ Set resource limits (memory, CPU, timeout)
     └─ Configure permission proxy

  3. Create core API
     ├─ Select API version based on manifest.spec.coreApiVersion
     ├─ Bind permissions from manifest.spec.permissions
     └─ Create storage & logger instances

  4. Load plugin module
     ├─ Read entry point (manifest.spec.entryPoint.main)
     ├─ Execute in sandbox
     └─ Validate exports

  5. Register hooks
     ├─ Scan manifest.spec.hooks
     ├─ Bind to exported functions
     └─ Sort by priority

  6. Execute onLoad hook
     ├─ Call exports.onLoad() if defined
     ├─ Wait with timeout (30s)
     └─ Catch errors, mark as failed if throws

  7. Record metrics
     ├─ Load time
     ├─ Memory usage
     └─ Timestamp

  Status: loaded
}
```

