## 15. Security Considerations

### 15.1 Threat Model

| Threat | Mitigation |
|--------|-----------|
| Plugin escapes sandbox | VM isolation, frozen prototypes |
| Plugin accesses unauthorized API | Permission proxy |
| Plugin crashes host | Error isolation, resource limits |
| Plugin exhausts memory | Memory ceiling enforced |
| Plugin makes external calls | Network permission required |
| Plugin steals user data | Restricted auth API |
| Supply chain attack | Optional code signature verification |

### 15.2 Signature Verification (Optional)

```bash
# Generate keypair for your organization
openssl genrsa -out signing-key.pem 4096
openssl rsa -in signing-key.pem -pubout > verification-key.pem

# Sign plugin package
npm run build
tar czf plugin.tar.gz dist/
openssl dgst -sha256 -sign signing-key.pem plugin.tar.gz > plugin.sig

# Install with signature verification
plugin install plugin.tar.gz --key verification-key.pem --signature plugin.sig
```

