## 8. Security & Sandbox Enforcement

### 8.1 Security Model

```typescript
interface SecurityModel {
  // 1. Permission-based access control
  permissions: PermissionPolicy;

  // 2. Resource limits
  limits: {
    memoryPerPlugin: number; // MB
    cpuTimePerCall: number; // ms
    networkConnectionsPerPlugin: number;
    fileSystemAccessAllowed: boolean;
    allowedNetworkDomains?: string[]; // Whitelist for external access
  };

  // 3. Code execution isolation
  isolation: {
    executionContext: 'vm' | 'worker' | 'process' | 'container';
    allowNativeModules: boolean;
    allowFileSystemAccess: boolean;
    allowNetworkAccess: boolean;
  };

  // 4. Audit and monitoring
  audit: {
    logAllApiCalls: boolean;
    captureArgs: boolean;
    captureResults: boolean;
    retentionDays: number;
  };

  // 5. Signature verification (optional)
  signing: {
    verifyPluginSignature: boolean;
    trustedPublishers: string[];
  };
}

// Default security configuration
const DEFAULT_SECURITY_CONFIG: SecurityModel = {
  permissions: {
    // Plugins must declare permissions in manifest
    // Admin approval for sensitive permissions
    requiresApprovalFor: ['access:database', 'access:external']
  },
  limits: {
    memoryPerPlugin: 256, // MB
    cpuTimePerCall: 30000, // ms
    networkConnectionsPerPlugin: 10,
    fileSystemAccessAllowed: false,
    allowedNetworkDomains: [] // Empty = no external access by default
  },
  isolation: {
    executionContext: 'worker', // Node.js Worker or Web Worker
    allowNativeModules: false,
    allowFileSystemAccess: false,
    allowNetworkAccess: false // Must be explicitly granted via permission
  },
  audit: {
    logAllApiCalls: true,
    captureArgs: false, // Set to true only if needed, can leak data
    captureResults: false,
    retentionDays: 90
  },
  signing: {
    verifyPluginSignature: false // Optional, can be enabled for enterprise
  }
};
```

### 8.2 Threat Mitigations

| Threat | Mitigation |
|--------|-----------|
| Resource exhaustion | Worker thread limits, memory caps, timeout enforcement |
| Privilege escalation | Permission gates, no access to host globals |
| Data exfiltration | Network domain whitelist, audit logging, no file system access |
| Code injection | Manifest validation, signature verification (optional), no dynamic require |
| Plugin conflicts | Conflict detection at load time, mutual exclusion |
| Dependency confusion | Dependency resolution with version pinning, registry lockfile |
| Supply chain attack | Signature verification, version pinning, deployment approval workflow |

### 8.3 Compliance Checklist

- [ ] All plugins declare permissions in manifest
- [ ] Permission changes require explicit admin approval
- [ ] Audit logs capture all API access with timestamp and plugin ID
- [ ] Resource limits are enforced and monitored
- [ ] Timeouts prevent hung processes
- [ ] No plugin can access another plugin's context
- [ ] Registry validates all manifests before registration
- [ ] Dependency cycles are detected and rejected
- [ ] Plugin source code is scanned for known vulnerabilities (optional)
- [ ] High-risk permissions trigger alerts

