### 6.3 Execution Modes

| Mode | Isolation Level | IPC Type | Use Case | Overhead |
|------|-----------------|----------|----------|----------|
| **In-Process** | Capability Whitelist | Direct | Trusted plugins, low latency | Minimal |
| **Worker Thread** | V8 Context | Message Pass | Untrusted, CPU-bound | Medium |
| **Child Process** | OS Process | Stdio/Socket | Complete isolation | High |
| **Remote (Network)** | Network Boundary | HTTP/gRPC | Third-party services | Very High |

### 6.4 Security Enforcement

```typescript
class SandboxBroker {
  // Prevents plugins from accessing platform internals
  private platformInternals = new Set([
    'process.env._INTERNAL_*',
    'global.__PLATFORM_STATE',
    'require.cache',
    'vm.runInNewContext', // no eval-like capabilities
  ]);

  // Whitelists what plugins can do
  createProxy(target: any, permissions: Permission[]): any {
    return new Proxy(target, {
      get: (obj, prop) => {
        if (this.platformInternals.has(prop)) {
          throw new SecurityViolationError(`Access to ${prop} denied`);
        }

        if (!this.hasPermission(permissions, 'read', prop)) {
          throw new PermissionDeniedError(`Cannot read ${prop}`);
        }

        return obj[prop];
      },

      set: (obj, prop, value) => {
        if (!this.hasPermission(permissions, 'write', prop)) {
          throw new PermissionDeniedError(`Cannot write ${prop}`);
        }
        obj[prop] = value;
        return true;
      },

      apply: (fn, thisArg, args) => {
        return fn.apply(thisArg, args); // wrapped with monitoring
      }
    });
  }
}
