## 9. Security Considerations

### 9.1 Trust Boundaries

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ Trust Zone: Platform Code & Core Team                       │
│ - No restrictions, direct access to internals              │
└──────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────┘
                           │
                   ╔═══════╩═══════╗
                   ║ Sandbox      ║
                   ║ Boundary     ║
                   ╚═══════╤═══════╝
                           │
┌──────────────────────────▼──────────────────────────────────┐
│ Trust Zone: Plugins                                         │
│ - Restricted access via capabilities                       │
│ - Resource limits enforced                                 │
│ - Audit logging on all operations                          │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

### 9.2 Threat Model

| Threat | Mitigation |
|--------|------------|
| **Malicious Code Injection** | Checksum verification, code signing, manifest validation |
| **Resource Exhaustion** | Memory/CPU/FD limits, rate limiting, circuit breakers |
| **Privilege Escalation** | Capability whitelisting, no eval, proxy enforcement |
| **Data Exfiltration** | Network whitelist, audit logging, encryption at rest |
| **Denial of Service** | Timeouts, request queues, health monitoring |
| **Dependency Attack** | Pinned versions, checksum verification, conflict detection |
| **Permission Escalation** | Explicit approval model, time-bound permissions, audit trail |

### 9.3 Security Checklist

- [ ] All plugins cryptographically signed by publisher
- [ ] Manifest integrity verified before loading
- [ ] Dependencies pinned to specific versions, not ranges
- [ ] All external calls logged with timestamp, user, args, result
- [ ] Capabilities explicitly approved by platform admin
- [ ] Network calls routed through proxy for inspection
- [ ] Database connections pooled and authenticated separately
- [ ] File access limited to designated directories
- [ ] Environment variables redacted from logs
- [ ] Plugins cannot modify their own manifest/capabilities
- [ ] Unload sequence enforces timeout and cleanup verification
- [ ] Regular security audits of plugin code (manual or automated)

