## 7. Hook Dispatcher

Routes hook invocations to registered plugin handlers with priority ordering.

### 7.1 Hook Registration

```typescript
export class HookDispatcher {
  /**
   * Register a hook handler from a plugin
   */
  register(
    hookName: string,
    handler: HookHandler<any>,
    options: {
      pluginId: string;
      priority: number; // Higher = earlier execution
      apiVersion: string;
    }
  ): void;

  /**
   * Unregister all handlers for a plugin
   */
  unregister(pluginId: string): void;

  /**
   * Dispatch hook to all registered handlers
   */
  async dispatch<T, R>(
    hookName: string,
    context: T
  ): Promise<DispatchResult<R>>;

  /**
   * Get handlers registered for a hook
   */
  getHandlers(hookName: string): HookHandlerInfo[];
}

export interface DispatchResult<R> {
  success: boolean;
  results: Array<{
    pluginId: string;
    result: HookResult;
    duration: number;
  }>;
  firstError?: PluginError;
}
```

### 7.2 Hook Execution Flow

```
1. dispatch(hookName, context)
   ├─ Find all handlers registered for hookName
   ├─ Sort by priority (descending)
   ├─ For each handler (in order):
   │  ├─ Create sandbox with handler's plugin config
   │  ├─ Execute: sandbox.executeHook(plugin, hookName, context)
   │  ├─ Capture: result, duration, errors
   │  └─ Continue (don't short-circuit on error)
   ├─ Aggregate results
   └─ Return DispatchResult
```

