## 13. Security Considerations

### 13.1 Threat Model

- **Malicious Code**: Mitigated by sandboxing & permissions
- **Privilege Escalation**: Plugins can't access host process
- **Data Exfiltration**: Network restricted; file I/O monitored
- **Resource Denial**: Memory/CPU/timeout limits enforced
- **Supply Chain**: Recommend author-signed plugins

### 13.2 Best Practices

1. Never trust manifest; validate at load time
2. Whitelist modules; deny by default
3. Audit permission grants
4. Isolate plugins in separate VM contexts
5. Kill runaway processes immediately
6. Sanitize context data before passing to plugins

