### **2. API Contract (Versioned)**

The core `Plugin` abstraction that all plugins extend:

```typescript
// v1.1 API - stable for 12 months minimum

export abstract class Plugin {
  abstract id: string;
  abstract version: string;

  // Lifecycle hooks (guaranteed 5s timeout for load, 3s for unload)
  abstract onLoad(): Promise<void>;
  abstract onUnload(): Promise<void>;
  onConfigChanged?(config: Record<string, any>): Promise<void>;

  // Hook implementations mapped by name
  getHooks(): Record<string, HookHandler<any>>;
}

// Host-provided API surface (injection at runtime)
export interface HostAPI {
  log(level: "info" | "warn" | "error", msg: string, ctx?: any): void;
  emit(event: string, data: any): Promise<void>;
  query(resource: string, filters?: Record<string, any>): Promise<any>;
  cache: {
    set(key: string, value: any, ttl?: number): Promise<void>;
    get(key: string): Promise<any>;
    del(key: string): Promise<void>;
  };
  getConfig(): Record<string, any>;
  measure(label: string, fn: () => Promise<void>): Promise<number>;
}

// Hook result wrapper (all hooks return this structure)
export interface HookResult {
  success: boolean;
  data?: any;
  error?: PluginError;
  warnings?: string[];
}

export class PluginError extends Error {
  constructor(
    public code: string,
    message: string,
    public details?: Record<string, any>
  ) {
    super(message);
  }
}
```

### **3. Lifecycle Manager (State Machine)**

```
discovered → registered → loading → loaded ↔ enabled/disabled
                            ↓ (error/timeout)
                          error (can retry)
```

**Lifecycle Methods**:
```typescript
class PluginLifecycleManager {
  async load(id: string, timeout?: number): Promise<PluginMetadata>
  async unload(id: string, timeout?: number): Promise<void>
  async reload(id: string): Promise<PluginMetadata>
  async enable(id: string): Promise<void>
  async disable(id: string): Promise<void>
  async updateConfig(id: string, config: any): Promise<PluginMetadata>

  on(event: LifecycleEvent, handler: any): () => void
}

type LifecycleEvent =
  | "plugin:discovered"
  | "plugin:loading"
  | "plugin:loaded"
  | "plugin:load-failed"
  | "plugin:unloading"
  | "plugin:unloaded"
  | "plugin:config-changed"
  | "plugin:error"
```

### **4. Sandboxed Execution Boundary**

Plugins execute in isolated Node.js VM contexts with enforced limits:

```typescript
class PluginSandbox {
  // Execute hook with resource limits
  async executeHook<T>(
    plugin: Plugin,
    hookName: string,
    context: T,
    hostAPI: HostAPI,
    config: SandboxConfig
  ): Promise<HookResult>
}

interface SandboxConfig {
  timeout: number;           // Kill after N ms
  memory: number;            // Max heap in bytes
  cpuQuota: number;         // 0-100%
  filesystem: {
    readOnly: boolean;
    allowedPaths: string[];
  };
  network: {
    enabled: boolean;
    allowedDomains: string[];
  };
  permissions: Set<string>; // Validated against manifest
}
```

**Isolation Strategy**:
- **Module Whitelist**: Only `util`, `path`, `url`, `querystring`, `buffer`, `crypto` (if declared)
- **Globals Denied**: No `process`, `require`, `global`, `fs`, `net`, `child_process`
- **Resource Limits**: Heap monitored; CPU yielding at hook boundaries; timeout enforcement
- **Error Isolation**: Hook errors caught; logged with plugin ID; don't crash host

### **5. Hook Dispatcher**

Routes invocations to registered handlers with priority-based ordering:

```typescript
class HookDispatcher {
  register(
    hookName: string,
    handler: HookHandler<any>,
    options: {
      pluginId: string;
      priority: number;        // Higher = earlier
      apiVersion: string;
    }
  ): void

  async dispatch<T>(
    hookName: string,
    context: T
  ): Promise<DispatchResult>
}

interface DispatchResult {
  success: boolean;
  results: Array<{
    pluginId: string;
    result: HookResult;
    duration: number;
  }>;
  firstError?: PluginError;
}
```

**Behavior**: Handlers execute in sequence by priority; failures don't short-circuit.

