## 10. Security Checklist

- [ ] **Manifest Validation**: Manifests validated against schema before registration
- [ ] **Capability Declaration**: Plugins must declare all capabilities; runtime enforces
- [ ] **Resource Limits**: Hard limits enforced; soft limits monitored
- [ ] **Isolation**: Plugin code runs in separate execution context (Worker/Isolate)
- [ ] **No Direct Host Access**: Plugins interact only via versioned API surface
- [ ] **Code Signing**: Plugins signed by publisher; signature verified at load time
- [ ] **Configuration Encryption**: Sensitive config fields encrypted at rest
- [ ] **Dependency Auditing**: Declared dependencies checked against vulnerability DB
- [ ] **Audit Logging**: All plugin operations logged for forensics
- [ ] **Rate Limiting**: API calls rate-limited per plugin
- [ ] **Timeout Enforcement**: Lifecycle hooks have mandatory timeouts
- [ ] **Health Monitoring**: Failed health checks trigger automatic unload

