## 12. Migration Path for Breaking Changes

When introducing API v2:

1. **Announce & Grace Period** (3 months): New version available, but v1 still supported
2. **Deprecation Warnings** (1 month): v1 plugins logged warnings on load
3. **Sunset** (major version bump): v1 no longer supported; all plugins must upgrade

```typescript
// Example: transitioning a method across versions
// v1 API
interface DataQueryAPIv1 {
  query(sql: string): Promise<DataTable>;
}

// v2 API (breaking change)
interface DataQueryAPIv2 {
  query(sql: string, options: QueryOptions): Promise<DataTable>;
  queryAsync(sql: string, options?: QueryOptions): AsyncIterator<DataRow>;
}

// Backward compat bridge (v1 plugins get wrapped calls)
class DataQueryBridge implements DataQueryAPIv1 {
  constructor(private v2: DataQueryAPIv2) {}

  async query(sql: string): Promise<DataTable> {
    return this.v2.query(sql, {});  // provide empty defaults for v1
  }
}
```

